  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.2. Increased capacity of Member States to apply international labour standards</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. The Zimbabwe United Nations Sustainable Development Cooperation Framework for 2022-2026 integrates actions to respond and implement comments of the ILO Supervisory Bodies: 
a. These actions are integrated under the PEACE PILLAR that seeks to advance Strategic Priority 4: on Transformative, accountable, equitable and inclusive governance. The work seeks to track the submission of reports to international treaty bodies and implementation of recommendations from commitments in normative
frameworks (e.g. CEDAW, Beijing, SADC protocol, Maputo protocol, CRC, CRPD, Refugee Convention/ Statelessness, UPR including ILO Supervisory Bodies).
2. The Zimbabwe Decent Work Country Programme for the period 2022 to 2026 signed and adopted in November 2022 integrates several outcomes that are linked directly to outcomes in the Zimbabwe United Nations Development Assistance Framework, 2022-2026. 
a. Outcome 2.2: International labour standards promoted for ratification and effective application that has an output that seeks to integrate principles of international labour standards and comments from the ILO supervisory bodies in sectoral and national policies/programmes links directly to  UNSDCF 4.1 Capacity of institutions and systems at national and sub-national levels is strengthened to discharge their mandate (human rights, rule of law, access to justice) in a transparent and accountable manner.
b. Two Outcomes are adopted directly from the UNSDCF into the DWCP-Outcome 1.1: All people in
Zimbabwe, especially the most vulnerable and marginalized, benefit from more inclusive and
sustainable economic growth with decent employment opportunities(UNSDCF Outcome 3) and DWCP Outcome 3.1: All people in Zimbabwe, especially women and girls and those in the most vulnerable and marginalized communities, benefit from equitable and quality social services and protection(UNSDCF Outcome 1). 1. The ILO has coordinated the participation of social partners in national consultations and report writing on CEDAW, UPR and ECOSOC. 
a. The ILO participates in the UNSDCF Peace Pillar and provides detailed inputs in the Pillar Workplan on follow-ups to comments and recommendations of ILO Supervisory Bodies.
2. The DWCP was developed after the adoption of the United Sustainable Development Cooperation Framework in which the ILO leads Pillar 3 on Prosperity and participates in the other Pillars on PEOPLE, PEACE and PLANET. Employment and decent work issues were integrated in the Common Country Assessment(CCA) and the results chain and workplans under the UNSDCF. 
c. The ILO coordinated the participation of social partners in the UNSDCF consultative process as part of wider consultations by the UN with civil society organisations.</narrative>
   </description>
